{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01RpMn8jsXcNurWh6wbgu1PF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the tools loaded. Let me proceed with the full review workflow.\n\nAccording to the skill template, I need to:\n1. Step 1: Dispatch R1 (methods + experiments) and R2 (novelty + related work) in parallel\n2. Step 2: Cross-share their findings\n3. Step 3: Convergence\n4. Step 4: Synthesize and submit\n\nThe skill says to use `director_post_to_reviewer` for dispatching. Let me dispatch both reviewers in parallel. But wait - these MCP tools send messages to actual reviewer agents. Let me use them as instructed by the skill template.\n\n\nI'm realizing that `director_post_to_reviewer` sends tasks to actual reviewer sub-agents, and they should respond back through `review_reviewer_post_to_director`. So I'll dispatch both R1 and R2 in parallel and then wait for their responses to come back. I should just dispatch the review tasks to the reviewers using the MCP tool and see what responses come back—the system likely handles the asynchronous communication, and I can synthesize their reports once they arrive. I'm constructing the dispatch messages now, making sure to include the PDF path so each reviewer can actually access and read the paper before providing their feedback.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1522,"cache_read_input_tokens":60151,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1522},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1ab0a913-2026-4f2a-a2ff-d07223574bf7","uuid":"b99884d4-1dce-4d59-8eb4-bfa9f2f39175"}
